// THE HARNESS TAKES A SEAT BEFORE IT TAKES A TURN. A serving group's seats are a pool on the
// fabric event log, one partition per group, whose root is the group's admitted engine tuple; the
// endpoint the turn talks to comes FROM the granted seat, never from a picker that could diverge
// from the admission (operator ruling 2026-09-06). A full group is a typed refusal, and the next
// group is tried; nothing queues. The reservation carries the declared maximum turn duration as
// its deadline, and the seat is released explicitly when the turn ends. Under vLLM the resource
// cannot fence a superseded holder, so the release law is quiescence-required: an expired seat
// whose turn was never seen to end stays held rather than becoming oversubscription.

fn harness_seat_partition(group: FabricGroup) -> PartitionId {
  join(["group-", fabric_group_wire(g: group) as String, "-seats"], "") as PartitionId
}

// THE SEAT CEILING IS NOT max_num_seqs, AND IT IS NOT DERIVED AT ALL YET.
//
// WHAT WAS HERE AND WHY IT WAS WRONG. This function read `a.max_num_seqs` off the desired engine
// and made it the pool ceiling. That is the engine's SCHEDULER COUNT LIMIT -- how many sequences it
// will admit to a batch -- and it is a different quantity from how much KV the fabric can hold.
// gunbc.spark.pair_serving_desired already states, at spark_pair_serving_seq_capacity, that NO LAW
// FROM POOL TOKENS TO ADMITTED SEQUENCES IS MODELLED; carrying 32 through to a capacity pool
// contradicted that in the same corpus, and every consumer of this pool then believed the fabric
// could seat 32 turns per group. That is fail-open in the exact wall the pool exists to hold.
//
// AND THE OBVIOUS REPLACEMENT IS ALSO FORBIDDEN. `num_gpu_blocks * block_size` is refused by
// construction at extdeps.vllm.kv_cache vllm_pool_reconstruction_is_authoritative
// (BlockCountTimesBlockSize => false), because under MLA with the DeepSeek fp8 layout it reports a
// small fraction of the logged pool. It has now been computed wrong three times in this repository,
// the third time by a reader who had the refusal in front of them. Neither is a seat count.
//
// NOR IS THE USAGE GAUGE A SATURATION SIGNAL. kv_cache_usage_perc counts RETAINED PREFIX-CACHE
// BLOCKS, so it reads high on an engine holding nothing: 96.5% at zero requests running
// (gunbc.spark.pair_serving_observed), reproduced live at 53% with zero running on the group B head.
// A seat law read off that gauge would be reading cache retention as occupancy.
//
// SO THE HONEST PRODUCTION RESULT IS THAT CAPACITY IS UNESTABLISHED, and the interim arm says
// OPERATOR POLICY in its own name so that no consumer, witness or receipt can read it as derived.
// The seats are a number the operator chose against observed concurrency; they are not a projection
// of any engine fact, and the moment the resolved-layout receipt exists this arm is deleted rather
// than re-grounded. The declared drop is gunbc.rung_drop harness_seat_ceiling_by_operator_policy.
type HarnessSeatCapacity
  = SeatCapacityByOperatorPolicy { pool: Pool<Count, One>, seats: Nat }
  | AdmissionCapacityUnestablished { group: FabricGroup, cause: NonEmptyStr }

// The operator's chosen interim seat count per serving group (2026-09-06), set against the
// concurrency actually observed running on the group A head. It is a POLICY CONSTANT: nothing
// derives it, and it carries no claim about what the KV pool can hold.
data harness_seat_operator_policy_seats: Nat = 3

fn harness_seat_capacity(group: FabricGroup) -> HarnessSeatCapacity {
  match spark_pair_serving_unit(group: group) {
    SparkPairServingUnitRefused { group: g, cause: _ } =>
      AdmissionCapacityUnestablished { group: g, cause: "the group's serving unit is refused, so it has no admitted engine to seat against" as NonEmptyStr }
    SparkPairServingUnitReady { group: _, engine: e, head: _, workers: _ } =>
      match e {
        VllmServing { args: _ } =>
          SeatCapacityByOperatorPolicy {
            pool: pool_of(
              identity: harness_seat_partition(group: group) as String as NonEmptyStr,
              ceiling: Measure { count: harness_seat_operator_policy_seats },
              replenishment: NoReplenishment,
            ),
            seats: harness_seat_operator_policy_seats,
          }
        OllamaServing { profile: _ } =>
          AdmissionCapacityUnestablished { group: group, cause: "the group is served by a runtime whose KV admission is not modelled" as NonEmptyStr }
      }
  }
}

// ── WHAT A PLACEMENT CAN ANSWER, AND WHY PENDING IS NOT A REFUSAL ─────────────────────────────
//
// Three arms, because the caller's remedies are three. BOUND is a seat on a named launch. PENDING is
// "every admissible group is busy right now": the demand is fine, the fleet is occupied, and a retry
// in a moment is the whole remedy. REFUSED is everything a retry does not fix -- no endpoint row, no
// admitted engine, an unreadable group, a selection that named an offer nothing can recover.
//
// FUSING PENDING INTO REFUSED WOULD MAKE PATIENCE LOOK LIKE A DEFECT, and worse, would make an
// unreadable group look like patience. An unread group frees nobody: nothing about waiting turns it
// into a reading, so its remedy is to go and measure.
type HarnessSeatBinding
  = HarnessSeatBound { url: String, grant: LeaseGrant, partition: PartitionId, group_wire: String, launch: VllmServingLaunch, work: ServingTurnWork<NonEmptyStr>, layout: EventLogLayout }
  | HarnessSeatPending { detail: String }
  | HarnessSeatRefused { detail: String }

fn seat_bind_detail(group: FabricGroup, text: String) -> String {
  join([fabric_group_wire(g: group) as String, ": ", text], "")
}

// ── THE HARNESS OFFERS ITS GROUPS AND ASKS THE FABRIC WHICH ONE WINS ──────────────────────────
//
// This fold USED to be the selection policy: walk the roster, take the first group that observed as
// serving and granted a seat. That made the harness a second placement authority beside the ctrl
// router's, and the two disagreed -- the router ranked by running requests and took no seat at all,
// so a turn it placed was invisible to this pool.
//
// A FIRST ATTEMPT TO FIX THAT MADE A THIRD ONE. It minted a serving-specific placement outcome, a
// serving-specific candidate and a serving-specific admissibility verdict, all of which already
// existed in product.fabric.selection as SupplySelection, CandidateOffer and OfferCandidacy -- and
// the re-minted admissibility was strictly weaker, a string reason where the fabric carries typed
// arms. It is not ported here, and it is not re-created here.
//
// What is left is what a consumer should have: observations in, a grant out. The harness supplies
// what it can see about each group, gunbc.serving.turn_admission decides which groups may be offered
// at all, product.fabric.selection ranks the survivors, and fabric_seat_acquire settles the race.
// Nothing in this module decides which group wins.
fn harness_serving_readiness(standing: HarnessBackendStanding, now: EpochSecs) -> SparkServingReadiness {
  match standing {
    HarnessBackendServing { model: _ } =>
      ServingObserved { ready_at: to_string(now), receipt: "gunbc.harness.models-probe" as ObservationReceiptRef }
    HarnessBackendModelAbsent { model: m, advertised: a } =>
      ServingUnobserved { obligation: join(["the replica advertises ", a, " and not ", m], "") as NonEmptyStr }
    HarnessBackendUnreachable { url: u } =>
      ServingUnobserved { obligation: join(["the replica at ", u, " did not answer"], "") as NonEmptyStr }
    HarnessBackendUnreadable { cause: c } =>
      ServingUnobserved { obligation: join(["the replica's model list was unreadable: ", c], "") as NonEmptyStr }
  }
}

// THE SEAT STANDING IS A READING, NOT A RETRY OUTCOME. Until fabric_seat_observe existed this path
// could only learn whether a pool had room by PROPOSING an acquire and being refused -- which costs
// an attempt and cannot be told apart from losing a race. A full group is a group that cannot start
// now, which is pending; an unreadable one is an obligation to go and measure.
type HarnessSeatStanding
  = SeatRoomForTurn
  | SeatPoolFull
  | SeatPoolUnread { obligation: NonEmptyStr }

fn harness_seat_standing(group: FabricGroup, layout: EventLogLayout, now: EpochSecs) -> HarnessSeatStanding {
  match harness_seat_capacity(group: group) {
    AdmissionCapacityUnestablished { group: _, cause: why } => SeatPoolUnread { obligation: why }
    SeatCapacityByOperatorPolicy { pool: root, seats: _ } =>
      match fabric_seat_observe(layout: layout, partition: harness_seat_partition(group: group), root: root, at: now, budget: 4096) {
        SeatStandingUnobserved { step: st, reason: why } =>
          SeatPoolUnread { obligation: join(["the seat pool could not be read at ", st, ": ", why], "") as NonEmptyStr }
        SeatFullObserved { generation: _ } => SeatPoolFull
        SeatRoomObserved { headroom: _, generation: _ } => SeatRoomForTurn
      }
  }
}

// ── WHAT THE TURN IS, WHICH THE SEAT CARRIES AND WHICH IS NOT COMPLETE TODAY ──────────────────
//
// The granted seat carries the Work it was granted for, and today that Work is a typed refusal: no
// observation in this repository establishes the exact model, tokenizer and runtime closure a launch
// loaded, so an inference turn has no canonical source manifest. Carrying the refusal is what keeps
// that visible at the point of use rather than filed somewhere nobody reads. What shipped before was
// to cast the served model ALIAS into the source manifest, which produced one Work identity for
// engines that may be serving different weights entirely.
fn harness_turn_request() -> ServingTurnRequest {
  ServingTurnRequest {
    source: serving_turn_source_unestablished(),
    runtime_closure: "gunbc.serving.runtime-closure-unobserved" as ArtifactManifestRef,
    inputs: "gunbc.serving.turn-inputs" as ArtifactManifestRef,
    effect_contract: "gunbc.serving.streamed-turn" as EffectContractRef,
    output_contract: "gunbc.serving.turn-completion" as OutputContractRef,
  }
}

// WHAT THE HARNESS REQUIRES, which must match what its own groups offer or nothing is fungible. The
// isolation profile is empty on BOTH sides deliberately: turns are not isolated from each other on a
// serving group, and a demand that pretended otherwise would refuse every offer we have.
fn harness_execution_requirements() -> ExecutionRequirements {
  serving_turn_requirements(
    capacity_class: ControlPlaneCapacity,
    capabilities: spark_serving_capability(model: harness_engine_model as NonEmptyStr),
    trust_domain: spark_serving_trust_domain,
    isolation: serving_isolation_profile(),
    shape: spark_serving_shape(),
  )
}

fn harness_turn_work() -> ServingTurnWork<NonEmptyStr> {
  serving_turn_work(principal: "gunbc" as NonEmptyStr, request: harness_turn_request(), requirements: harness_execution_requirements())
}

fn harness_turn_work_standing(w: ServingTurnWork<NonEmptyStr>) -> String {
  match w {
    TurnWorkBound { work: work } => join(["work ", work.id.key as String], "")
    TurnWorkUnestablished { obligation: o } => join(["work unestablished: ", o as String], "")
  }
}

// ── A CANDIDATE IS AN OFFER PLUS WHAT IT TAKES TO ACT ON IT ───────────────────────────────────
//
// The launch and the address travel beside the candidate rather than being recovered from the offer
// key by taking a prefix of it. An offer key is one opaque name, and a consumer that parses it has
// made its shape load-bearing.
type HarnessCandidate {
  key: NonEmptyStr
  group: FabricGroup
  address: String
  launch: VllmServingLaunch
  offer: CandidateOffer<NonEmptyStr>
}

type HarnessCandidates {
  candidates: List<HarnessCandidate>
  notes: List<String>
  retryable: Bool
}

fn harness_no_candidate(acc: HarnessCandidates, note: String, retryable: Bool) -> HarnessCandidates {
  HarnessCandidates { candidates: acc.candidates, notes: concat(acc.notes, [note]), retryable: acc.retryable || retryable }
}

fn harness_bind_candidate(acc: HarnessCandidates, group: FabricGroup, address: String, launch: VllmServingLaunch, now: EpochSecs) -> HarnessCandidates {
  match bind_spark_serving_offer(
    principal: "gunbc" as NonEmptyStr,
    executor: fabric_group_wire(g: group),
    launch: launch,
    model: harness_engine_model as NonEmptyStr,
    trust_domain: spark_serving_trust_domain,
    isolation: serving_isolation_profile(),
    seats: harness_seat_operator_policy_seats as Int,
    readiness: harness_serving_readiness(standing: harness_observe_replica(address: address), now: now),
  ) {
    SparkOfferBindingRefused { group_wire: _, cause: why } =>
      harness_no_candidate(acc: acc, note: seat_bind_detail(group: group, text: why as String), retryable: false)
    SparkOfferBound { bound: projection } =>
      match bind_candidate(
        offer: projection.offer,
        dispatch: serving_dispatch_inputs(
          offer: projection.offer.id,
          commitment: PayAsYouGo,
          receipt: "gunbc.harness.offer-bind" as ObservationReceiptRef,
        ),
      ) {
        DispatchInputsNameAnotherOffer { offer: _, inputs_name: _ } =>
          harness_no_candidate(acc: acc, note: seat_bind_detail(group: group, text: "the dispatch inputs named another offer"), retryable: false)
        CandidateBound { candidate: c } =>
          HarnessCandidates {
            candidates: concat(acc.candidates, [HarnessCandidate { key: vllm_serving_launch_key(launch: launch), group: group, address: address, launch: launch, offer: c }]),
            notes: acc.notes,
            retryable: acc.retryable,
          }
      }
  }
}

// ADMISSION HAPPENS BEFORE THE OFFER IS BOUND, WHICH IS THE POINT OF THE CUT. An occupied group is
// not a worse candidate; it is not a candidate. The earlier design bound it, priced its co-tenancy
// on the opportunity axis and let the ranking decide -- which places the arriving prefill beside a
// live decode whenever the alternatives happen to look worse.
fn harness_add_candidate(acc: HarnessCandidates, group: FabricGroup, address: String, layout: EventLogLayout, now: EpochSecs) -> HarnessCandidates {
  let engine = harness_observe_engine(group: group, address: address)
  match engine.launch {
    LaunchUnobserved { group: _, obligation: o } =>
      harness_no_candidate(acc: acc, note: seat_bind_detail(group: group, text: o as String), retryable: false)
    LaunchObserved { launch: launch, receipt: _ } => {
      let admission = serving_group_admission(tenancy: serving_co_tenancy(reading: engine.queue), receipt: "gunbc.harness.metrics-probe" as ObservationReceiptRef)
      if !serving_admission_is_admissible(admission: admission) {
        harness_no_candidate(acc: acc, note: serving_admission_detail(group: group, admission: admission), retryable: serving_admission_is_retryable(admission: admission))
      } else {
        match harness_seat_standing(group: group, layout: layout, now: now) {
          SeatPoolUnread { obligation: o } =>
            harness_no_candidate(acc: acc, note: seat_bind_detail(group: group, text: o as String), retryable: false)
          SeatPoolFull =>
            harness_no_candidate(acc: acc, note: seat_bind_detail(group: group, text: "every seat in the group's pool is held, so it cannot start this turn now"), retryable: true)
          SeatRoomForTurn =>
            harness_bind_candidate(acc: acc, group: group, address: address, launch: launch, now: now)
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

// EXCLUDED KEYS ARE EXCLUDED BY EXACT LAUNCH IDENTITY, which is what makes a reselect after a lost
// race sound: the offer that lost is the offer on that launch, and if the engine has restarted
// since, the group returns under a different key and is a candidate again rather than being shunned
// for its predecessor's contention.
fn harness_is_excluded(excluded: List<String>, key: NonEmptyStr) -> Bool {
  any(excluded, k => k == (key as String))
}

fn harness_collect_candidates(layout: EventLogLayout, now: EpochSecs, excluded: List<String>) -> HarnessCandidates {
  let collected = fold(spark_pair_serving_groups, init: HarnessCandidates { candidates: [], notes: [], retryable: false }, f: (acc, g) =>
    match host_lan_address(host: spark_pair_serving_head(group: g)) {
      Absent => harness_no_candidate(acc: acc, note: seat_bind_detail(group: g, text: "head has no LAN endpoint row"), retryable: false)
      Present { value: address } => harness_add_candidate(acc: acc, group: g, address: address as String, layout: layout, now: now)
    })
  HarnessCandidates {
    candidates: filter(collected.candidates, c => !harness_is_excluded(excluded: excluded, key: c.key)),
    notes: collected.notes,
    retryable: collected.retryable,
  }
}

fn harness_candidate_for_key(candidates: List<HarnessCandidate>, key: NonEmptyStr) -> HarnessCandidate? {
  first(filter(candidates, c => (c.key as String) == (key as String)))
}

// ── THE COMPARE-AND-SET REMAINS THE ARBITER, AND LOSING IT IS NOT THE END ─────────────────────
//
// Selection decides which offer is preferred from what was observed; the seat can still be taken
// between that reading and this acquire, and when it is, the acquire refuses. That race is not a
// defect in the policy -- it is why the policy does not try to settle it.
//
// WHAT WAS MISSING WAS THE OTHER HALF. The lost race was returned to the caller as a terminal
// inability to place the demand, when it is ordinary contention: another request took the seat, and
// the remaining offers were never asked. A lost compare-and-set therefore excludes that launch and
// reselects over what is left, bounded, with the groups re-observed each round because the world
// moved -- the group that was occupied a moment ago may now be free, and the one that was free may
// have restarted.
type HarnessAcquisition
  = AcquisitionGranted { binding: HarnessSeatBinding }
  | AcquisitionLost { key: NonEmptyStr, detail: String }
  | AcquisitionRefused { detail: String }

// ── THE GRANT IS FENCED AGAINST THE LAUNCH IT WAS TAKEN FOR ───────────────────────────────────
//
// Naming the launch on the offer keeps a dead engine's evidence from pricing its successor between
// ROUNDS. It does not, by itself, cover the window inside one round: the engine can be replaced
// after selection reads it and before the seat is taken, and the seat would then authorize a request
// against an engine that never answered a probe -- a fresh KV cache, a different effective policy,
// possibly a different runtime. Restart is exactly the event that invalidates an outstanding grant,
// so the grant is checked against the launch it was taken for, once, at the point it is issued.
//
// A CHANGED LAUNCH RELEASES THE SEAT AND IS ORDINARY CONTENTION. The successor is a different offer
// subject and may be perfectly good; excluding this launch and reselecting is what the bounded loop
// already does for a lost compare-and-set, and the group returns under its new key on the next
// round. Holding the seat while refusing would leak it.
//
// AN UNREADABLE ENGINE HERE REFUSES RATHER THAN RETRYING, because a group that stopped answering
// between selection and acquisition frees nobody by being waited for.
fn harness_fence_grant(candidate: HarnessCandidate, layout: EventLogLayout, partition: PartitionId, shape: HarnessWireShape, grant: LeaseGrant, now: EpochSecs) -> HarnessAcquisition {
  match harness_observe_engine(group: candidate.group, address: candidate.address).launch {
    LaunchUnobserved { group: _, obligation: o } => {
      let released = release_retry(layout: layout, partition: partition, reference: grant.reference, reason: "the engine could not be identified after the seat was granted" as NonEmptyStr, now: now)
      AcquisitionRefused { detail: seat_bind_detail(group: candidate.group, text: join([o as String, " (seat ", harness_seat_release_wire(r: released), ")"], "")) }
    }
    LaunchObserved { launch: current, receipt: _ } =>
      if vllm_serving_launch_is(launch: current, other: candidate.launch) {
        AcquisitionGranted {
          binding: HarnessSeatBound {
            url: harness_backend_url_for_address(shape: shape, address: candidate.address),
            grant: grant,
            partition: partition,
            group_wire: fabric_group_wire(g: candidate.group) as String,
            launch: candidate.launch,
            work: harness_turn_work(),
            layout: layout,
          },
        }
      } else {
        let released = release_retry(layout: layout, partition: partition, reference: grant.reference, reason: "the engine was replaced between selection and acquisition" as NonEmptyStr, now: now)
        AcquisitionLost {
          key: candidate.key,
          detail: seat_bind_detail(group: candidate.group, text: join(["the engine was replaced between selection and acquisition (seat ", harness_seat_release_wire(r: released), ")"], "")),
        }
      }
  }
}

fn harness_acquire_on(candidate: HarnessCandidate, layout: EventLogLayout, shape: HarnessWireShape, actor: NonEmptyStr, policy: LeasePolicy, now: EpochSecs) -> HarnessAcquisition {
  match harness_seat_capacity(group: candidate.group) {
    AdmissionCapacityUnestablished { group: _, cause: why } =>
      AcquisitionRefused { detail: seat_bind_detail(group: candidate.group, text: why as String) }
    SeatCapacityByOperatorPolicy { pool: root, seats: _ } => {
      let partition = harness_seat_partition(group: candidate.group)
      let request = SeatRequest {
        reference: join([actor as String, "@", to_string(now)], "") as NonEmptyStr,
        amount: 1,
        at: now,
        term_seconds: policy.maximum_duration_seconds,
      }
      match fabric_seat_acquire(layout: layout, partition: partition, root: root, actor: actor, request: request, policy: policy, attempts: 3, budget: 4096) {
        SeatGranted { grant: g, generation: _, attempts_used: _ } =>
          harness_fence_grant(candidate: candidate, layout: layout, partition: partition, shape: shape, grant: g, now: now)
        SeatFull { wire: w, attempts_used: _ } =>
          AcquisitionLost { key: candidate.key, detail: seat_bind_detail(group: candidate.group, text: w) }
        SeatContended { attempts: a } =>
          AcquisitionLost { key: candidate.key, detail: seat_bind_detail(group: candidate.group, text: join(["the seat compare-and-set was contended ", to_string(a), " times"], "")) }
        SeatAcquireRefused { step: st, reason: why, attempts_used: _ } =>
          AcquisitionRefused { detail: seat_bind_detail(group: candidate.group, text: join([st, ": ", why], "")) }
      }
    }
  }
}

// THE ENDPOINT COMES FROM THE ACQUIRED OFFER, NEVER FROM A PICKER. The url on a bound seat is the
// address of the candidate that won selection and then won the compare-and-set. A second lookup here
// -- asking the roster for a serving address again, say -- would be a placement decision taken after
// the placement decision, and the two are free to disagree exactly when a group has just restarted.

type PlacementRound {
  done: HarnessSeatBinding?
  excluded: List<String>
  notes: List<String>
  retryable: Bool
}

fn harness_nothing_placed(notes: List<String>, retryable: Bool) -> HarnessSeatBinding {
  if retryable {
    HarnessSeatPending { detail: join(["no serving group can take this turn now: ", join(notes, "; ")], "") }
  } else {
    HarnessSeatRefused { detail: join(["no serving offer was admissible: ", join(notes, "; ")], "") }
  }
}

fn harness_placement_round(acc: PlacementRound, layout: EventLogLayout, shape: HarnessWireShape, actor: NonEmptyStr, policy: LeasePolicy, now: EpochSecs) -> PlacementRound {
  match acc.done {
    Present { value: _ } => acc
    Absent => {
      let collected = harness_collect_candidates(layout: layout, now: now, excluded: acc.excluded)
      let notes = concat(acc.notes, collected.notes)
      let retryable = acc.retryable || collected.retryable
      match select_supply(
        requirements: harness_execution_requirements(),
        candidates: map(collected.candidates, c => c.offer),
        duration: EstimatedGrantDuration { seconds: policy.maximum_duration_seconds },
        maximum_buy_order: money_amount_micro(count: 0),
        budget_currency: Usd,
        delay_valuation: serving_delay_valuation,
        tie: DemandKeyedRendezvous,
        demand_key: actor,
      ) {
        NoAdmissibleOffer { considered: _ } =>
          PlacementRound {
            done: Present { value: harness_nothing_placed(notes: notes, retryable: retryable) },
            excluded: acc.excluded,
            notes: notes,
            retryable: retryable,
          }
        EqualCostTieUnresolved { digest: d, considered: _ } =>
          PlacementRound {
            done: Present { value: HarnessSeatRefused { detail: join(["two serving offers produced the same rendezvous digest ", d as String, ", so the tie policy could not choose between them"], "") } },
            excluded: acc.excluded,
            notes: notes,
            retryable: retryable,
          }
        OfferSelected { offer: o, cost: _, basis: _, horizon: _, considered: _, tie_policy: _ } =>
          match harness_candidate_for_key(candidates: collected.candidates, key: o.id.key) {
            Absent =>
              PlacementRound {
                done: Present { value: HarnessSeatRefused { detail: join(["selection returned an offer key naming no candidate: ", o.id.key as String], "") } },
                excluded: acc.excluded,
                notes: notes,
                retryable: retryable,
              }
            Present { value: c } =>
              match harness_acquire_on(candidate: c, layout: layout, shape: shape, actor: actor, policy: policy, now: now) {
                AcquisitionGranted { binding: b } =>
                  PlacementRound { done: Present { value: b }, excluded: acc.excluded, notes: notes, retryable: retryable }
                AcquisitionRefused { detail: d } =>
                  PlacementRound { done: Present { value: HarnessSeatRefused { detail: d } }, excluded: acc.excluded, notes: notes, retryable: retryable }
                AcquisitionLost { key: k, detail: d } =>
                  PlacementRound { done: none, excluded: concat(acc.excluded, [k as String]), notes: concat(notes, [d]), retryable: true }
              }
          }
      }
    }
  }
}

data harness_placement_rounds: Nat = 3

// NO ADMISSIBLE OFFER IS A REFUSAL OR A PENDING, NEVER A DEGRADED PATH. The arm this replaces walked
// the roster and took whatever granted a seat, which is the same shape as the router's "the request
// has to go somewhere".
fn harness_bind_seat(short_hostname: String, shape: HarnessWireShape, actor: NonEmptyStr, policy: LeasePolicy) -> HarnessSeatBinding {
  match event_log_layout_for_host(short_hostname: short_hostname) {
    HostLayoutRefused { detail: d } => HarnessSeatRefused { detail: d }
    HostLayoutResolved { layout: layout, executor: _ } =>
      match now_epoch_seconds() {
        Absent => HarnessSeatRefused { detail: "the clock could not be read as epoch seconds" }
        Present { value: now } => {
          let placed = fold(nat_range_inclusive(lo: 1, hi: harness_placement_rounds), init: PlacementRound { done: none, excluded: [], notes: [], retryable: false }, f: (acc, _i) =>
            harness_placement_round(acc: acc, layout: layout, shape: shape, actor: actor, policy: policy, now: now))
          match placed.done {
            Present { value: b } => b
            Absent =>
              HarnessSeatPending { detail: join(["every selected seat was taken by another request within ", to_string(harness_placement_rounds), " rounds: ", join(placed.notes, "; ")], "") }
          }
        }
      }
  }
}

// RELEASE IS AN EVENT ON THE SAME PARTITION, appended against the head observed at release time
// and retried on stale, because the seat's neighbours keep moving the head while this turn ran.
type HarnessSeatRelease
  = HarnessSeatReleased { partition: PartitionId }
  | HarnessSeatReleaseRefused { detail: String }

type ReleaseFold {
  done: HarnessSeatRelease?
}

fn release_append(layout: EventLogLayout, partition: PartitionId, reference: NonEmptyStr, reason: NonEmptyStr, now: EpochSecs) -> HarnessSeatRelease? {
  match event_log_observe_head(layout: layout, partition: partition) {
    HeadObservationRefused { step: s, reason: why } => Present { value: HarnessSeatReleaseRefused { detail: join([s, ": ", why], "") } }
    HeadObserved { head: head } => {
      let event = ChainEvent {
        partition: partition,
        parent: match head { HeadAbsent => none  HeadAt { id: h } => Present { value: h } },
        recorded_at: now,
        actor: reference,
        payload: PoolReleased { reference: reference, reason: reason },
      }
      match event_log_append(layout: layout, partition: partition, event: event, expected: head) {
        EventAppended { id: _ } => Present { value: HarnessSeatReleased { partition: partition } }
        EventAppendStale { expected: _, observed: _ } => none
        EventAppendRefused { step: s, reason: why } => Present { value: HarnessSeatReleaseRefused { detail: join([s, ": ", why], "") } }
      }
    }
  }
}

fn release_retry(layout: EventLogLayout, partition: PartitionId, reference: NonEmptyStr, reason: NonEmptyStr, now: EpochSecs) -> HarnessSeatRelease {
  let st = fold(nat_range_inclusive(lo: 1, hi: 3), init: ReleaseFold { done: none }, f: (acc, _i) =>
    match acc.done {
      Present { value: _ } => acc
      Absent => ReleaseFold { done: release_append(layout: layout, partition: partition, reference: reference, reason: reason, now: now) }
    })
  match st.done {
    Present { value: r } => r
    Absent => HarnessSeatReleaseRefused { detail: "release contended three times" }
  }
}

fn harness_release_seat(binding: HarnessSeatBinding, reason: NonEmptyStr) -> HarnessSeatRelease {
  match binding {
    HarnessSeatRefused { detail: d } => HarnessSeatReleaseRefused { detail: join(["nothing to release: ", d], "") }
    HarnessSeatPending { detail: d } => HarnessSeatReleaseRefused { detail: join(["nothing to release, the placement is pending: ", d], "") }
    HarnessSeatBound { url: _, grant: g, partition: p, group_wire: _, launch: _, work: _, layout: layout } =>
      match now_epoch_seconds() {
        Absent => HarnessSeatReleaseRefused { detail: "the clock could not be read as epoch seconds" }
        Present { value: now } => release_retry(layout: layout, partition: p, reference: g.reference, reason: reason, now: now)
      }
  }
}

// ── RELEASING A SEAT SOMEONE ELSE'S PROCESS HOLDS ─────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// A turn taken through the harness releases its own seat: the binding is in hand and the process
// that acquired it is the process that ends it. A turn proxied by the ROUTER cannot do that, because
// the grant is handed out across a process boundary -- so the release has to be reachable from the
// three facts that travel with the grant: which host holds the event log, which group's partition
// the seat is in, and the grant reference.
//
// IT IS THE SAME APPEND, NOT A SECOND RELEASE PATH. release_append is the one place a PoolReleased
// event is written, and both entries reach it. A separate writer here would be a second authority
// over the pool's history, free to write an event the fold does not expect.
//
// THE REFERENCE IS NOT VALIDATED AGAINST THE HOLDER, and that is stated rather than hidden: this
// releases the seat named by the reference it is given. The pool's fold is what refuses a release of
// something never acquired; a caller that passes another actor's reference releases that actor's
// seat, exactly as an operator releasing a stuck seat by hand would. Fencing that is a lease
// question and it is not answered here.
fn harness_group_for_wire(group_wire: String) -> FabricGroup? {
  first(filter(spark_pair_serving_groups, g => (fabric_group_wire(g: g) as String) == group_wire))
}

fn harness_release_reference(short_hostname: String, group_wire: String, reference: NonEmptyStr, reason: NonEmptyStr) -> HarnessSeatRelease {
  match harness_group_for_wire(group_wire: group_wire) {
    Absent => HarnessSeatReleaseRefused { detail: join(["no serving group is wired as ", group_wire], "") }
    Present { value: g } =>
      match event_log_layout_for_host(short_hostname: short_hostname) {
        HostLayoutRefused { detail: d } => HarnessSeatReleaseRefused { detail: d }
        HostLayoutResolved { layout: layout, executor: _ } =>
          match now_epoch_seconds() {
            Absent => HarnessSeatReleaseRefused { detail: "the clock could not be read as epoch seconds" }
            Present { value: now } =>
              release_retry(layout: layout, partition: harness_seat_partition(group: g), reference: reference, reason: reason, now: now)
          }
      }
  }
}

fn harness_seat_release_wire(r: HarnessSeatRelease) -> String {
  match r {
    HarnessSeatReleased { partition: p } => join(["released on ", p as String], "")
    HarnessSeatReleaseRefused { detail: d } => join(["release refused: ", d], "")
  }
}

fn harness_now_epoch() -> EpochSecs? {
  now_epoch_seconds()
}
